    sffi_authority_census_ambient_call_gap_2026-08-24, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: demonstrated the gap with a doc-constructed fixture (ambient rt_env_get call with no local extern and no sffi import produced no census row; the doc's named mir_text_codegen call is gone at this base per its own 2026-11-13 addendum). Root cause: sffi-call-authority-census.shs built each file's raw-name set only from local extern declarations and sffi imports, then skipped files with no such declarations - ambient-only files were invisible (a lower-bound inventory). Fix (scripts/audit/sffi-call-authority-census.shs): generic rt_*/spl_* alternative always enters the per-file call regex with a cheap per-line candidate flag; match-time classification adds an ambient state for names not in the declared/imported set; locally defined pure-Simple fn/me rt_* names excluded (with a shadow-guard for body-local extern re-declarations found on the real tree); summary gains ambient_call_sites + an explicit partial-coverage label; symbols/families/scopes/files tables gain an ambient_calls column; the missing ratchet and baseline untouched. After: selftest PASS with new ambient + pure-local + mixed-shadow fixtures; full tree exit 0, raw_call_sites 20,277 to 22,217 (+1,940 rows ALL ambient: top linalg/backend_ops.spl 215, blas_openblas.spl 123), 0 rows removed, missing identical at 14,636 (set-diff verified). Runtime ~38s (was seconds) - one linear pass, recorded per the perf rule. Residual per doc: resolved-HIR identity / aliased-provider ownership / cross-runtime contract (acceptances 3-5) need the HIR-based inventory owned by the SFFI authority lane; ambient rows are lexical and may include cross-file pure-helper false positives - now visible and triageable. close_evidence reproducer=scripts/audit/sffi-call-authority-census.shs prevention=scripts/audit/sffi-unsafe-backlog.shs"

